<title>USA: St Louis feeder cattle prices firm-up $2 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Louis feeder cattle prices firm-up $2 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>EAST ST LOUIS, Ill. 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>FEEDER CATTLE</p>
<p>AUCTION: 225 head. Compared with last week feeder steers and</p>
<p>heifers were firm to $2.00 per cwt higher, USDA said. Overall</p>
<p>quality was comparable to last week. Moderate buyer</p>
<p>attendance. Receipts 225  Last week-no report- Last Year-250</p>
<p>FEEDER STEERS: Medium and Large Frame 1:</p>
<p>500-600 lbs. 83.00-90.00, Crossbreds  90.00-94.00</p>
<p>600-700 lbs. 79.00-85.00, Crossbreds  85.00-88.00</p>
<p>700-800 lbs. 75.00-80.00</p>
<p>Moderately Fleshy:  800-1050 lbs. 63.00-70.00</p>
<p>Large Frame 2 Holsteins: 1150-1250 lbs. 51.00-52.00</p>
<p>FEEDER HEIFERS:  Medium and Large Frame 1:</p>
<p>500-600 lbs. 76.00-81.00, Crossbreds 81.00-83.00</p>
<p>700-800 lbs. 70.00-75.00, pkg. gaunt 760 lb. Crossbreds 81.50</p>
<p>Moderately Fleshy: 600-900 lbs. 62.00-69.00</p>
<p>Cow/calf pairs:  Part load large frame 3-5 years old with</p>
<p>calves at side 730.00/pair.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
